// Spawnable — the trait role of a deferred-work LAUNCHER (the C# shape;
// see docs/ASYNC.md, "Design decisions"). A Spawnable class packs a deferred unit of work
// (the construction special form) and its `start` submits it, yielding the
// library-owned `Task<T>` handle — so the await half is guaranteed by the
// return type and each type carries exactly one role: `Thread<T>`/`Fiber<T>`
// are spawnable, `Task<T>` is awaitable. `Awaitable` stays non-generic (its
// `wait` does not mention T); `Spawnable` is generic because `start`'s
// return type does.
//
// `detach` is the daemon role: run the work unjoinable, statement only.

/**
 * A class that can launch a deferred call and hand back its Task<T> handle
 **/
pub trait Spawnable<T> {
	func start = (ref self, move out Task<T>)
	func detach = (ref self)
}
